{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> \"Go out now\" — like \"now.\"" "<b>Shear-jashub.</b> The name of the prophet's son, as I will explain. Those who say [it means] \"your son\" from the root בינה have no understanding in grammar." "<b>Te'alah.</b> Like \"which was in the channel\" (1 Kings 18:38), and the mem is a root letter, and the spelling is not thus, for the te'alah is a place where rainwater gathers. And our Rabbis said it is so called because its waters are from a blessed place [ממקום מבורך]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra quotes the rabbinic etymology (from ברך); the bracketed correction [צ\"ל ממקום] reflects a manuscript reading noted in standard editions; translated as transmitted."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:34.160136461Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}